    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d710">

                <pb facs="1018" n="898" xml:id="pg898"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/2552: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul at Harbin</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Hanson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-06-15T16:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 15, 1922—4
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>For Stevens:</p>
                <p>Your May 25, 8 a.m. and Department’s May 27, 5 p.m.<anchor n="74"
                        xml:id="d710-f1"/> I have about concluded that further expenditure of
                    American funds in connection with the Chinese Eastern and Trans-Siberian
                    Railways at this time is not advisable and contemplate so notifying governments
                    concerned within the near future. Before doing so, however, I should like to
                    have by telegraph any suggestions you can make in the premises especially with
                    respect to possible arrangements for securing American interests and your
                    estimate of approximate amount of funds which will remain on immediate winding
                    up.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d710-f1" n="74" xml:id="d710-f1-content">
